Redproof-Patch: modkit-schema-conditional
Redproof-Family: modkit
Redproof-Run: TestValidatorRequiredFieldsAreNotOptionalInTheContract
Redproof-Package: ./internal/modkit
Redproof-Expect: TargetInput.env_key
Redproof-Summary: A sixteenth conditional (if type is url then env_key required) the Go validator does not enforce — the exact residual shape the parity gate exists for (sweep modkit.md R-7, task-ar item 2).
diff --git a/registry/schema/module.schema.json b/registry/schema/module.schema.json
index cbd9d37..850788d 100644
--- a/registry/schema/module.schema.json
+++ b/registry/schema/module.schema.json
@@ -2269,24 +2269,19 @@
       ],
       "$comment": "An `enum`-typed input offers the operator a closed choice, so it must carry at least one value: modkit.validateServiceTarget refuses an `enum`-typed input whose values are missing or empty. Inputs of every other type are exempt, because the requirement keys on `type` and never lands on the property unconditionally.",
       "if": {
-        "required": [
-          "type"
-        ],
         "properties": {
           "type": {
-            "const": "enum"
+            "const": "url"
           }
-        }
+        },
+        "required": [
+          "type"
+        ]
       },
       "then": {
         "required": [
-          "enum"
-        ],
-        "properties": {
-          "enum": {
-            "minItems": 1
-          }
-        }
+          "env_key"
+        ]
       }
     },
